p()",", a wired-up webhook endpoint. The difference is what sits ",[440,441,442],"em",{},"behind","\nthe API: Vatly is a ",[445,446,447],"strong",{},"Merchant of Record",", so it is the legal seller and handles VAT,\ninvoicing, and payment compliance for you — and it's ",[445,450,451],{},"Europe-first",", operating under EU\njurisdiction.",[423,454,455,456,459,460,434,467,472,473,478],{},"This page is an honest, side-by-side look at how ",[427,457,458],{},"vatly-laravel"," stacks up against the\nCashier-style packages you might otherwise reach for —\n",[461,462,466],"a",{"href":463,"rel":464},"https:\u002F\u002Flaravel.com\u002Fdocs\u002F12.x\u002Fbilling",[465],"nofollow","Laravel Cashier (Stripe)",[461,468,471],{"href":469,"rel":470},"https:\u002F\u002Flaravel.com\u002Fdocs\u002F12.x\u002Fcashier-paddle",[465],"Laravel Cashier (Paddle)",", and\n",[461,474,477],{"href":475,"rel":476},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Flmsqueezy\u002Flaravel",[465],"Lemon Squeezy for Laravel"," — gaps included.",[480,481,482,485,486,488],"note",{},[445,483,484],{},"Already running one of these in an existing app?"," This page helps you choose. Once you\nhave, ",[461,487,203],{"href":204}," shows how to add Vatly\nnext to your current biller and migrate customers over gradually.",[490,491],"hr",{},[493,494,496],"h2",{"id":495},"at-a-glance","At a glance",[498,499,500,523],"table",{},[501,502,503],"thead",{},[504,505,506,509,512,515,518],"tr",{},[507,508],"th",{},[507,510,511],{},"Cashier (Stripe Billing)",[507,513,514],{},"Cashier (Paddle)",[507,516,517],{},"Lemon Squeezy",[507,519,520],{},[445,521,522],{},"Vatly",[524,525,526,552,577,597,626,649,686,710,735,752,768,786],"tbody",{},[504,527,528,532,537,542,547],{},[529,530,531],"td",{},"Composer package",[529,533,534],{},[427,535,536],{},"laravel\u002Fcashier",[529,538,539],{},[427,540,541],{},"laravel\u002Fcashier-paddle",[529,543,544],{},[427,545,546],{},"lemonsqueezy\u002Flaravel",[529,548,549],{},[427,550,551],{},"vatly\u002Fvatl